    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/advisor-for-student-success/": {
      "title": "Advisor for Student Success",
      "description": "Advisor for Student Success – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Advisor for Student Success POSITION: Full-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-08-03 15:48:56 Position Summary The Advisor for Student Success supports the mission of the Student Success Center by fostering student achievement, persistence, and personal growth through proactive advising, intentional programming, collaborative campus partnerships, first-year student education, and coordinated student support initiatives. The Advisor will empower students to develop the skills, confidence, and connections needed to thrive academically, socially, and personally throughout their college experience. The Student Success Center’s goal is to ensure all students have the support needed to be as successful as possible while at West Virginia Wesleyan College. Advisors accomplish this by empowering students in three key areas: ● Academics – Helping students create and implement academic plans, develop effective learning strategies, and utilize campus resources. ● Engagement and Belonging – Encouraging participation in campus opportunities that foster meaningful relationships and a strong sense of community. ● Self-Advocacy and Support Seeking – Guiding students to develop confidence in advocating for themselves and connecting with appropriate campus resources when needed. The Advisor provides individualized student support, assists in designing and implementing student success programming, develops marketing and outreach initiatives, and collaborates with the Director to teach First-Year Experience (FYEX) courses that equip new students with the knowledge and skills necessary for a successful transition to college. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide proactive, holistic advising to assigned students through individual meetings, outreach, and follow-up. Assist students in developing academic success strategies, including time management, goal setting, study skills, and academic planning. Monitor student progress and identify students who may benefit from additional support or intervention. Connect students with appropriate campus resources, faculty, and staff. Maintain accurate records of student interactions and referrals. Co-teach First-Year Experience (FYEX) courses with the Director of the Student Success Center Assist in evaluating program effectiveness using participation data, surveys, and student feedback Develop engaging marketing materials for Student Success Center initiatives using print and digital platforms. Create content for social media, email campaigns, digital signage, and campus communications. Maintain a consistent and welcoming brand identity for the Student Success Center. Promote student success resources through creative outreach strategies that increase awareness and participation. Participate on institutional committees related to student engagement and success. Collect and analyze student participation and success data. Assist with assessment reports and strategic planning initiatives. Recommend improvements based on assessment findings and student feedback. Support institutional retention and persistence goals. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s degree preferred Minimum of 2 years advising experience To Apply: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, resume and names and contact information of three references to wvwcjobapp@wvwc.edu.  On the subject of the email, please enter:  ##3## – Advisor for Student Success. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. West Virginia Wesleyan College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, ancestry, marital/family status, veteran status, sexual orientation, sex characteristics,  pregnancy, religion, age, disability or blindness, or any other characteristic protected by local, state or federal law , to include Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, Section 504, and the Age Discrimination Act, in the administration of its admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, educational programs, employment, athletic programs, co-curricular activities, or other College administered programs. WVWC’s nondiscrimination polices may be accessed at https://www.wvwc.edu/title-ix/ . For inquiries about the application of these laws in WVWC’s programs activities or to file a report, contact the Title IX Coordinator at titleix@wvwc.edu or 304-621-1316. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Policies Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/graduate-assistant-for-sports-information/": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Sports Information",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Sports Information – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions Housing About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Graduate Assistant for Sports Information POSITION: Part-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-07-12 07:45:00 West Virginia Wesleyan College is seeking one (1) individual for the position of Graduate Assistant for Sports Information. A member of NCAA Division II and the Mountain East Conference, West Virginia Wesleyan College sponsors 22 intercollegiate sports. The Sports Information Graduate Assistant (GA) position is a 10-month graduate assistant position beginning August 1, 2026 and reports to the Sports Information Director. The GA will assist the Sports Information Department in the management of rosters, schedules, statistics, story writing and online media content creation for all 22 West Virginia Wesleyan Athletics programs. The GA will assist with gameday duties to prepare, conduct and recap home athletic events. The individual in this position will work twenty hours per week and must remain as a full-time student in good academic standing. Successful candidates must be accepted into one of West Virginia Wesleyan College’s graduate programs. The Sports Information GA will be an integral member of the WVWC Athletics Department regarding the planning and implementation of athletics content to engage supporters and promote teams and athletes. Additionally, this position will assist the department of compliance, and perform relevant duties regarding game operations and general athletics office support. Position Responsibilities: Assist in the management of rosters, schedules, and statistics for all 22 Athletics programs through the NCAA, the Mountain East Conference and the Bobcats website: com Write previews, recaps, and personal interest stories for the Bobcats website and other local, regional and national media. Assist in the creation and management of all West Virginia Wesleyan Athletics media, including photography, graphics, and video. Assist in the production of live broadcasts for all home competitions. Use social media platforms to enhance the reach of content, and engagement. Report to the Sports Information Director to assist in the planning and execution of Athletics events. Assist Compliance and Athletics Office upon request and other duties as assigned. Position Requirements and Preferred Experience: Bachelor’s degree in a related field (Sports Management, Communications, Business Administration, Marketing) Acceptance into one of WVWC’s graduate programs: https://www.wvwc.edu/graduate-programs/ Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills Strong journalistic writing ability and knowledge of AP style Proficiency in media creation software such as Photoshop, Canva or Box Out Sports. Wesleyan uses Box Out for the creation of social media posts. Experience with NCAA LiveStats (Genius Sports) software Broadcasting experience (play-by-play or color commentary) Diligent and organized working habits Position Benefits : Graduate Assistants will receive: Full tuition On Campus Housing Campus meal plan 10-month stipend To Apply: Review of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Candidates must submit the following electronically – letter of application, resume, portfolio (as applicable), and two references with contact information to Sports Information Director, Rigel Wilson at sportsinfo@wvwc.edu. Please enter “ your last name -Sports Information GA” on the subject line of the email. Located in Buckhannon, W.Va., West Virginia Wesleyan features a beautiful 100-acre campus of red-brick Georgian architecture. West Virginia Wesleyan was also named one of the best colleges in the South by U.S. News & World Report. West Virginia Wesleyan College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, ancestry, marital/family status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, religion, age, disability or blindness, or any other characteristic protected by local, state or federal law , to include Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, Section 504, and the Age Discrimination Act, in the administration of its admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, educational programs, employment, athletic programs, co-curricular activities, or other College administered programs. WVWC’s nondiscrimination polices may be accessed at https://www.wvwc.edu/title-ix/ .   For inquiries about the application of these laws in WVWC’s programs activities or to file a report, contact the Title IX Coordinator at titleix@wvwc.edu or 304-621-1316. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Policies Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
    "https://www.wvwc.edu/jobs/custodian/": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian – West Virginia Wesleyan College Skip to content Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give Home Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Visit Affordability International Transfer Commit to WVWC Financial Aid & Scholarships Students Academic Calendar Support Campus Life Community Engagement Student Accounts About About WVWC Campus Offices Conferences, Events, and Camps Consumer Information Contact Jobs News Academics Undergraduate Majors Graduate Programs Registrar Resources Alumni Athletics Give 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 Admissions About Students Alumni Give Contact 59 College Ave.         Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000 about Job Listings Custodian POSITION: Full-Time DATE POSTED: 2026-04-23 20:18:16 West Virginia Wesleyan College is seeking a full-time, 12-month, Custodian. RESPONSIBILITIES OF POSITION: Perform housekeeping and cleaning of all facilities. The essential and marginal functions include: housekeeping of college facilities, performing set-up for special events, securing and unlocking buildings as required, inventory functions, and material requisition for supplies and any additional duties or job descriptions as assigned by administrative personal of West Virginia Wesleyan College. QUALIFICATION REQUIREMENTS: Ability to read, write, and understand oral and written communications. Working knowledge in the use of custodial equipment and power tools, i.e. buffers, burnishers, scrubbing unit, carpet equipment, etc. Must be knowledgeable of environmental products and their applications and disposal procedures. Must be able to climb step ladders. 1-year experience in the custodian trade (for new hire only). WORKING CONDITIONS: Requires ability to lift 25-50 lbs., climb ladders, twist bend knees, prolonged standing, sweeping and mopping, vacuuming, use power tools, and visually and manually inspect work being preformed on campus as needed. Exposure to cleaning products, dust, and dirt on a daily basis. Potential exposure to blood-borne pathogens. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT: As determined by the Collective Bargaining Agreement and West Virginia Wesleyan College. EVALUATION: Performance of this position will be evaluated annually. TO APPLY: Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest, resume and names and contact information of three references to wvwcjobapp@wvwc.edu.  On the subject of the email, please enter:  ##7## – Custodian. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Equal Opportunity Policy West Virginia Wesleyan College is an equal opportunity employer. It is the policy of the College to create a favorable work environment in which all employees, regardless of race, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, disability, or religious affiliation, can enjoy equal opportunities in their employment relationship with the College. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Policies Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
    },
