duation, etc.) as needed. Some evenings may be needed. Assist with graphic design and photography needs Assist with webpage creation and updates as needed Monitor media outreach/social media impressions Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree Acceptance to one of WVWC’s graduate programs Some social media or digital content creation experience is preferred This position will run August 1 – May 31.  The graduate assistant will work 20 hours a week and must remain a full-time student and be in good academic standing. Interested applicants should send a resume and cover letter to Amanda Hayes, Associate Director of Marketing and Communication, at hayes.a@wvwc.edu. West Virginia Wesleyan College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, creed, ancestry, marital/family status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, religion, age, disability or blindness, or any other characteristic protected by local, state or federal law , to include Title VI, Title VII, Title IX, Section 504, and the Age Discrimination Act, in the administration of its admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, educational programs, employment, athletic programs, co-curricular activities, or other College administered programs. WVWC’s nondiscrimination polices may be accessed at https://www.wvwc.edu/title-ix/ .   For inquiries about the application of these laws in WVWC’s programs activities or to file a report, contact the Title IX Coordinator at titleix@wvwc.edu or 304-621-1316. About Wesleyan Contact Current Livestream Events Title IX Consumer Info Non-Discrimination Statement Privacy Policies Library Shop News Potential Students Request Info Virtual Tour Visit Current Students Bobcat Connect eCampus Bookstore Blackboard Academic Support Academic Calendar Jobs Self-Service Self-Service Alumni Give ABU Resources Bobcat Beacon West Virginia Wesleyan College 59 College Ave. Buckhannon, WV 26201 (304)-473-8000"
